                                        "glosses": [
                                            "counterattack"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "552a850b-1ff1-4119-8849-83d268066a80",
                                                "sense_id": "5671e954-7ddb-3572-b51d-a27b0d5fbde7",
                                                "text": "Arsenal lacked urgency and penetration in a lazy, lacklustre opening half, sucked in by Forest's strategy of sitting back in blocks of defence waiting to hit them on the counter."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "counter",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "46de752f-7e94-3887-b30b-a60ce9a504ec",
                                        "entry_id": "a4efe0ce-a1d2-3371-80a8-1b456653f6cf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To contradict, oppose."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55108a0e-1d9c-42ba-b2ce-2f45f288e7c9",
                                                "sense_id": "46de752f-7e94-3887-b30b-a60ce9a504ec",
                                                "text": "I don't remember the conversation totally verbatim, yet I remember the tone — increasingly angry on my part, and flippant and snide on his. We countered back and forth at least three times."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e4a684a-71a7-45e6-9595-95b87c76bc2b",
                                                "sense_id": "46de752f-7e94-3887-b30b-a60ce9a504ec",
                                                "text": "In a war of words that has broken out between Khan and Secretary of State for Transport Grant Shapps, the Mayor was accused of sending revenue-raising proposals to Shapps some three weeks late, giving him little choice but to extend negotiations. Khan countered this by alleging that 'unfair' conditions, such as raising council tax, are being attached to any new funding deal that would \"punish Londoners\" for the effect the pandemic has had on passenger numbers. He added: \"These short-term deals are trapping TfL on life support rather than putting it on the path to long-term sustainability.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "142a432a-bb18-39e1-9034-dbfde14c8637",
                                        "entry_id": "a4efe0ce-a1d2-3371-80a8-1b456653f6cf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To return a blow while receiving one, as in boxing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2cdf7563-dcd0-4bdf-b2ea-cb58cb0a8aac",
                                                "sense_id": "142a432a-bb18-39e1-9034-dbfde14c8637",
                                                "text": "His left hand countered provokingly."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "870f2d56-e46c-3deb-a192-9bb06e198095",
                                        "entry_id": "a4efe0ce-a1d2-3371-80a8-1b456653f6cf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To take action in response to; to respond."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29209307-081b-4520-b0b7-31f532e064e2",
                                                "sense_id": "870f2d56-e46c-3deb-a192-9bb06e198095",
                                                "text": "David Cameron insists that his latest communications data bill is “vital to counter terrorism”. Yet terror is mayhem. It is no threat to freedom. That threat is from counter-terror, from ministers capitulating to securocrats."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f93a2fc7-1888-3f47-89b5-7fe1d590c2be",
                                        "entry_id": "a4efe0ce-a1d2-3371-80a8-1b456653f6cf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To encounter."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "counter",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "45f436d5-29f3-3a3d-bae3-2c67152b2448",
                                        "entry_id": "73446065-9f75-3445-889e-19d64e2fbd83",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Contrary or opposing"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3ba2ca4f-c4d0-45a0-b1e8-468361260e0b",
                                                "sense_id": "45f436d5-29f3-3a3d-bae3-2c67152b2448",
                                                "text": "His carrying a knife was counter to my plan."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3cf7a639-eeb5-4ac8-aeba-4b5f5bc78e43",
                                                "sense_id": "45f436d5-29f3-3a3d-bae3-2c67152b2448",
                                                "text": "He could not compel Mrs. Proudie to say that the report was untrue; nor could he condescend to make counter hits at her about her own daughter, as his wife would have done."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96d3e2c0-0f3f-4ce1-b6e9-2a765c94c8a4",
                                                "sense_id": "45f436d5-29f3-3a3d-bae3-2c67152b2448",
                                                "text": "Innumerable facts attesting the counter principle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "718d7110-c4b4-45f8-8f67-a8007bc5d9c1",
                                                "sense_id": "45f436d5-29f3-3a3d-bae3-2c67152b2448",
                                                "text": "It was, however, most interesting work, and the moulders themselves were a decent crowd, never tired of making jokes about themselves such as the hoary one that moulders did not live long, which however ran counter to the other one that no germs could live in a foundry—the atmosphere was too foul."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
